// Jutland, 31 May 1916 at 14:00 GMT (docs/battle/plan.md step 2.7: the scale test). The order of battle is the
// historical one, ship by ship; the classes are stand-ins (Designs/, knob variants of the shipped designs, until a
// ship design session). The British dispositions are the 2 p.m. ones of Jellicoe's despatch and the Admiralty's
// Narrative of the Battle: Lion in 56°46'N 4°40'E, just turned N by E at 19.5 kn to meet the Grand Fleet, the 2nd BCS
// 3 miles ENE of her, the 5th Battle Squadron 5 miles NNW, the light cruisers a screen 8 miles astern on a line
// ENE-WSW, 5 miles apart (the 1st LCS at its eastern end, as Galatea's 14:25 position, 56°48'N 5°21'E, has it);
// the battle fleet in 57°57'N 3°45'E, organisation No. 5 (six columns of divisions, 1st to 6th port to starboard),
// steering S 50 E at a 14-knot speed of advance, the 4th LCS 3 miles ahead, the cruisers 16 miles ahead and 8 apart,
// Hood's 3rd BCS with Chester and Canterbury about 20 miles ahead. The German positions are reckoned from the
// contact, not logged: Hipper fifty miles east of Beatty steering north, Elbing on his screen's western wing some
// 17 miles east of Galatea (the steamer N. J. Fjord between them), Scheer fifty miles astern of Hipper. Galatea
// sights Elbing's torpedo boats at the steamer at 14:20 and the first shots are at 14:28.
